//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// Apex 50K Eval Lab  (TradingView Pine Script v6 strategy)
// =============================================================================
//
// WHAT THIS IS
//   A backtest research lab built to answer one question honestly: if a
//   signal had been run on an Apex Trader Funding 50K Intraday Trailing
//   Drawdown evaluation, attempt after attempt through the chart's history,
//   how often would an attempt have passed, compared with random entries that
//   have no edge but use the same session window, sizing, costs, exits and
//   account rules?
//
//   This is a lab. It is NOT a live signal and NOT advice, and nothing it
//   shows is a recommendation to place a trade. It has no alerts. Results on
//   past bars do not predict future results, and a result is only as good as
//   the model described below.
//
// RULES MODELLED (from trading/apex-50k/rules.json, verifiedOn 2026-11-01)
//   Evaluation: start 50,000; profit target +3,000 on closed P&L (open profit
//   does not count); trailing drawdown 2,000 from the peak balance INCLUDING
//   open profit; the threshold never moves down and stops rising at 53,000 on
//   Rithmic/WealthCharts (it keeps trailing on Tradovate); the account is
//   breached when the balance touches or falls below the threshold; maximum
//   6 minis or 60 micros; no daily loss limit; 30 calendar days of access.
//   Performance Account (PA): threshold stops rising at 50,100; contract cap
//   and daily loss limit come from the scaling tier set by the prior
//   session's closing balance (never below Level 1):
//     L1 profit 0 -> 2 minis, DLL 1,000     L2 1,500 -> 3 minis, DLL 1,000
//     L3 3,000 -> 4 minis, DLL 2,000        L4 6,000 -> 4 minis, DLL 3,000
//   A DLL hit flattens and pauses the rest of the session; the PA stays open.
//   Sources (re-check them before relying on any number; the firm can change
//   its rules at any time):
//     https://apextraderfunding.com/help-center/evaluation-accounts-ea/intraday-trailing-drawdown-evaluations/
//     https://apextraderfunding.com/help-center/intraday-trailing-drawdown-accounts/intraday-trailing-drawdown-explained/
//     https://apextraderfunding.com/help-center/additional-helpful-items/position-sizing-evaluation
//     https://apextraderfunding.com/help-center/intraday-trailing-drawdown-accounts/intraday-trailing-drawdown-performance-accounts-pa/
//     https://apextraderfunding.com/help-center/additional-helpful-items/scaling-levels-pa-explained/
//     https://apextraderfunding.com/help-center/intraday-trailing-drawdown-accounts/intraday-trailing-drawdown-payouts/
//
// HOW TO USE
//   1. Open MNQ1! or NQ1! (or one specific contract month) on a 1 to 5 minute
//      chart. The default $100 risk per trade suits MNQ; on NQ ($20/point) a
//      $100 budget covers only stops under about 4.9 points, so at the default
//      8-point July min stop EVERY July setup is skipped for size (and most
//      1-ATR external and random entries too). On NQ set Risk per trade to at
//      least about $162 (8 pt x $20 + $1.50 round trip), or chart MNQ.
//   2. Add this strategy and open the Strategy Tester. The table at the top
//      right is the lab's result: attempts, passes, breaches and expiries for
//      the signal ledger and for the random control, split into attempts whose
//      first trading day is before the out-of-sample date and attempts whose
//      first trading day is on or after it.
//   3. Pick the signal source: the built-in July NQ setups, an external
//      indicator's plot (value > 0 long, < 0 short, 0 none), or the random
//      control only (the strategy itself then trades the random entries,
//      which also cross-checks the random ledger against TradingView fills).
//   4. Compare the signal's pass rate with the random control's, above all on
//      out-of-sample attempts. A signal that does not clearly beat random
//      there has not shown an edge. A handful of attempts is anecdote, not a
//      rate; the counts are shown so the sample size can be judged.
//   5. Raw trades for the planner (any firm, e.g. a Tradeify 50K funded
//      account): set Account mode to "Raw trades (no account rules)". There
//      are then no attempts and no account ledger: every signal the source
//      produces while flat is taken, sized by risk per trade as above and
//      capped by "Max contracts in raw mode" (default 4 minis, 40 micros on a
//      micro symbol: the Tradeify 50K limit). For Tradeify set the flat-by
//      time to 16:40 (Tradeify requires flat by 16:45 ET). Set Exit model to
//      "Fixed R" for an export: with "July playbook" each exit leg is its own
//      List of trades row, and the planner sizes, caps and steps each row on
//      its own, never the combined position, so it overstates size and
//      understates breach risk (the table warns). The export's P&L uses the
//      Properties tab commission, so set that to your real commission per
//      side per contract first. Then:
//        a. Strategy Tester > List of trades > Export, saved as list.csv.
//        b. From trading/apex-50k, run the planner, which applies the firm's
//           rules itself and resizes each trade by its risk (--scale risk):
//             node planner/cli.mjs --firm tradeify --plan growth --trades list.csv --unit micro --sweep --scale risk
//           (--unit mini for an NQ export, but on NQ set Risk per trade to at
//           least about $162 first or no July setup is taken (see 1); MNQ
//           with --scale risk is simpler. Drop --firm and --plan for Apex.)
//      The table then shows trades, win %, net P&L per trade per contract,
//      profit factor and net P&L for the signal and the random control,
//      in-sample and out-of-sample.
//
// HOW THE LEDGER COUNTS
//   - Each attempt starts at 50,000 on the first bar of a trading session
//     (18:00 ET for CME futures) once the ledger is flat; after a pass,
//     breach or expiry the next attempt starts at the next session. Attempts
//     never overlap. The first attempt waits for indicator warm-up.
//   - Every bar the ledger observes the balance (closed P&L net of costs plus
//     open P&L) at the bar's extremes, limited to what the position could see
//     while its stop and targets were working, then at the close.
//   - Pass: flat with closed P&L >= +3,000. Expiry: 30 calendar days after
//     the attempt's first trading day. "Days to pass" counts traded sessions
//     (sessions with at least one entry), as Apex counts trading days.
//   - Performance Account mode has no target: an attempt ends on a breach or
//     when it has survived the PA horizon (input, in sessions), and a fresh
//     one starts. The table shows the share of finished attempts breached
//     within the horizon and the median traded days to breach; the attempt
//     still running is shown only in the current-attempt rows.
//   - Raw trades mode has no ledger. A trade is one position from entry to
//     flat, with all its exit legs summed (the List of trades shows each leg
//     of a July-playbook split as its own row, which the planner reads as a
//     separate trade, so export with Fixed R exits). Its P&L is net of the lab's
//     cost model, its contracts are the entry size, and it is in-sample or
//     out-of-sample by the trading day of its entry (CME roll, 18:00 ET).
//     Net P&L per trade per contract is the average over trades of each
//     trade's net P&L divided by its contracts; profit factor is gross profit
//     over gross loss in dollars as traded.
//
// LIMITS
//   - History: TradingView limits intraday bar history by subscription plan,
//     so the number of attempts available depends on the plan.
//   - Intrabar order is unknown on OHLC bars. By default the ledger observes a
//     bar's FAVOURABLE extreme first (raising peak and threshold), then its
//     ADVERSE extreme (breach check), then the close: the worst case for an
//     intraday trailing threshold. "Adverse first" is offered as an option.
//   - Fills: signals are evaluated on bar close only and entries fill at the
//     next bar's open with 1 tick of slippage; stops fill with 1 tick of
//     slippage (at the open if price gaps through); targets fill at the limit.
//   - The strategy's fills come from TradingView's broker emulator, which
//     resolves a bar that touches both stop and target with its own OHLC path
//     rule. The random control resolves such bars stop-first by default. The
//     table counts these bars for both ledgers; set the random control's rule
//     to "TradingView OHLC path" for a like-for-like comparison.
//   - Costs: both ledgers are charged the lab's commission model (input; auto
//     = $0.75 per side per mini, $0.25 per side per micro). The Strategy
//     Tester's own P&L uses the Properties-tab commission (declared $0.75);
//     the lab ledger removes that and applies its own model, so the table and
//     the Strategy Tester can differ by the commission difference.
//   - Breach, daily-loss-limit and flat-by exits are market orders that fill
//     at the next bar's open, so a realised loss can run past the level that
//     triggered it. The ledger's verdict comes from the observed touch.
//   - Flat-by is capped at Apex's 16:59 ET deadline and is sent on the last
//     bar whose close (the next bar's open, where it fills) is at or before
//     the flat-by time, so it lands in time on any intraday timeframe.
//   - Holiday early closes are not scheduled: a position still open on a
//     session's last bar, or carried into a new session, is closed at that
//     bar's close.
//   - Not modelled: payout, consistency, news and inactivity rules.
//   - 15-minute bias uses request.security with lookahead on and a [1]
//     offset: the last completed 15-minute bar, the same on historical and
//     live bars, never the future. On the last chart bar inside a 15-minute
//     bar it is one 15-minute bar older than the bar that has just closed.
//   - Prior-day high/low are built on the chart from the trading day's bars
//     (request.security("D", high[1]) with lookahead off would return the
//     day before yesterday on historical bars).
//   - July setups follow the Python engine (signals.py, indicators.py,
//     market.py, playbook.py): best candidate by score, then the score,
//     stop-size and net-R gates. Lunch is not blocked (the engine treats it as
//     a soft warning; its -15 score penalty still applies).
// =============================================================================

strategy("Apex 50K Eval Lab", shorttitle = "ApexEvalLab", overlay = true,
     initial_capital = 50000, currency = currency.USD,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1,
     pyramiding = 0, process_orders_on_close = false,
     calc_on_every_tick = false, calc_on_order_fills = false,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.75,
     slippage = 1, margin_long = 0, margin_short = 0,
     max_labels_count = 5, max_lines_count = 5, max_boxes_count = 5)

// <<RULES:BEGIN>>
// Apex 50K Intraday Trailing Drawdown. Values must match rules.json exactly
// (na = null in rules.json: no stop / no limit; FLAT_BY_ET_MIN = flatByEt in
// minutes after midnight ET).
float START_BAL = 50000
float EVAL_TARGET = 3000
float EVAL_DD = 2000
float EVAL_STOP_RITHMIC = 53000
float EVAL_STOP_TRADOVATE = na
float EVAL_DLL = na
int EVAL_MAX_MINIS = 6
int EVAL_ACCESS_DAYS = 30
float PA_DD = 2000
float PA_STOP = 50100
float PA_T2_PROFIT = 1500
float PA_T3_PROFIT = 3000
float PA_T4_PROFIT = 6000
int PA_T1_MINIS = 2
int PA_T2_MINIS = 3
int PA_T3_MINIS = 4
int PA_T4_MINIS = 4
float PA_T1_DLL = 1000
float PA_T2_DLL = 1000
float PA_T3_DLL = 2000
float PA_T4_DLL = 3000
int MICROS_PER_MINI = 10
int FLAT_BY_ET_MIN = 1019
// <<RULES:END>>

// ------------------------------------------------------------ constants ----
TZ = "America/New_York"
int DAY_MS = 86400000
int WARMUP_BARS = 200
int SLIP_TICKS = 1          // must equal the slippage set in the strategy declaration above

int ST_IDLE = 0
int ST_ACTIVE = 1
int ST_PASSED = 2
int ST_BREACHED = 3
int ST_EXPIRED = 4

int REG_UP = 1
int REG_DOWN = 2
int REG_CHOP = 3
int REG_EXP = 4
int REG_QUIET = 5

SRC_JULY = "July NQ setups"
SRC_EXT = "External indicator"
SRC_RAND = "Random control only"
EXIT_FIXED = "Fixed R"
EXIT_JULY = "July playbook"
ORD_FAV = "Conservative (favorable first)"
ORD_ADV = "Adverse first"
AMB_STOP = "Stop first (conservative)"
AMB_TV = "TradingView OHLC path"
COMM_AUTO = "Auto by symbol class"
COMM_CUSTOM = "Custom"
MODE_RAW = "Raw trades (no account rules)"

// --------------------------------------------------------------- inputs ----
grpAcct = "Apex account"
iMode = input.string("Evaluation", "Account mode", options = ["Evaluation", "Performance Account", MODE_RAW], group = grpAcct,
     tooltip = "Raw trades: no attempts and no account rules. Every signal is taken with the same sizing, window, exits and flat-by, so the List of trades can be exported to the planner for any firm.")
iFeed = input.string("Rithmic/WealthCharts", "Data feed", options = ["Rithmic/WealthCharts", "Tradovate"], group = grpAcct,
     tooltip = "Evaluation only. Rithmic/WealthCharts: the threshold stops rising at 53,000. Tradovate: it keeps trailing. A Performance Account always stops at 50,100.")
iOrder = input.string(ORD_FAV, "Intrabar ordering", options = [ORD_FAV, ORD_ADV], group = grpAcct,
     tooltip = "Order in which the ledger observes each bar's extremes. Favorable first raises the peak and threshold before the adverse extreme is checked: the worst case for a trailing threshold.")
iPaHorizon = input.int(20, "PA horizon (sessions)", minval = 1, group = grpAcct,
     tooltip = "Performance Account only. An attempt that has not breached after this many sessions ends as survived and a fresh one starts, so the breach rate is the share of attempts breached within this many sessions.")

grpSig = "Signal"
iSource = input.string(SRC_JULY, "Signal source", options = [SRC_JULY, SRC_EXT, SRC_RAND], group = grpSig,
     tooltip = "Random control only: the strategy itself trades the random-control entries (same generator), which also cross-checks the random ledger against TradingView fills.")
iUseTP = input.bool(true, "Trend Pullback", group = grpSig)
iUseORB = input.bool(true, "Opening Range Breakout", group = grpSig)
iUseVR = input.bool(true, "VWAP Reclaim", group = grpSig)
iUseFB = input.bool(true, "Failed Breakout Reversal", group = grpSig)
iUseFade = input.bool(true, "VWAP Fade", group = grpSig)
iMinScore = input.float(55.0, "Minimum setup score (0-100)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 5, group = grpSig)
iMinStop = input.float(8.0, "July min stop (points)", minval = 0, step = 1, group = grpSig)
iMaxStop = input.float(60.0, "July max stop (points)", minval = 1, step = 5, group = grpSig)
iMinNetR = input.float(1.2, "July min net R to target 1 (after costs)", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = grpSig)
iExtSrc = input.source(close, "External signal", group = grpSig,
     tooltip = "Choose another indicator's plot. Read on bar close: value > 0 long, < 0 short, 0 none. If that indicator repaints, so will the result.")
iExtAtr = input.float(1.0, "External signal stop (ATR multiple)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpSig)

grpExit = "Exits"
iExit = input.string(EXIT_FIXED, "Exit model", options = [EXIT_FIXED, EXIT_JULY], group = grpExit,
     tooltip = "Fixed R: one stop and one target at the R multiple. July playbook: half off at target 1 (1.5R), stop to breakeven once 1R is touched, the rest at the setup's target 2 (2.5R for external and random entries). A single contract exits whole at target 1. For a raw-trades export to the planner use Fixed R: July legs export as separate trades.")
iRMult = input.float(2.0, "Fixed R target (R multiple)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.25, group = grpExit)

grpRisk = "Risk and costs"
iRisk = input.float(100.0, "Risk per trade ($)", minval = 1, step = 25, group = grpRisk,
     tooltip = "Stop distance x point value + round-trip cost per contract decides size. $100 is 5% of the 2,000 drawdown.")
iMaxQty = input.int(0, "Max contracts override (0 = plan cap)", minval = 0, group = grpRisk,
     tooltip = "In contracts of the charted symbol. Never exceeds the plan cap (Evaluation 6 minis / 60 micros; PA tier cap; Raw trades: Max contracts in raw mode).")
iCommMode = input.string(COMM_AUTO, "Commission model", options = [COMM_AUTO, COMM_CUSTOM], group = grpRisk,
     tooltip = "Auto: $0.75 per side per mini contract, $0.25 per side per micro. Charged to both ledgers.")
iCommCustom = input.float(0.75, "Custom commission per side per contract ($)", minval = 0, step = 0.05, group = grpRisk)

grpSess = "Session (America/New_York)"
iWindow = input.session("0935-1530", "New entries window", group = grpSess,
     tooltip = "An entry is allowed when its fill time (the signal bar's close) is inside this window.")
iFlatH = input.int(16, "Flat-by time (hour : minute)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = grpSess, inline = "fb")
iFlatM = input.int(55, "", minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = grpSess, inline = "fb",
     tooltip = "Positions are closed by this time: the market close is sent on the last bar whose close is at or before it and fills at the next bar's open. Capped at 16:59 ET, Apex's flat-by deadline. Tradeify requires flat by 16:45 ET, so use 16:40 for Tradeify exports.")
iOOS = input.time(timestamp("01 Aug 2026 00:00 -0400"), "Out-of-sample start", group = grpSess,
     tooltip = "Attempts whose first trading day is before this date (ET) are in-sample; on or after it, out-of-sample. The default is after the July setups were written.")

grpRnd = "Random control"
iRndProb = input.float(0.03, "Entry probability per eligible bar", minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.01, group = grpRnd)
iRndAtr = input.float(1.0, "Stop (ATR multiple)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpRnd)
iSeed = input.int(12345, "Seed", group = grpRnd)
iAmb = input.string(AMB_STOP, "Bar touching stop and target", options = [AMB_STOP, AMB_TV], group = grpRnd,
     tooltip = "How the random control resolves a bar that touches both its stop and a target. The strategy's fills always follow TradingView's OHLC path rule.")

grpDisp = "Display"
iShowTable = input.bool(true, "Show results table", group = grpDisp)

// Declared last so the inputs above keep their positions (saved settings).
grpRaw = "Raw trades mode"
iRawMaxMinis = input.int(4, "Max contracts in raw mode (minis)", minval = 1, group = grpRaw,
     tooltip = "Raw trades mode only. In minis: on a micro symbol each mini is 10 micros, so the default 4 is 4 NQ or 40 MNQ, the Tradeify 50K limit. Max contracts override, when set, still applies.")

// -------------------------------------------------------- symbol & costs ----
var array<string> MICRO_ROOTS = array.from("MNQ", "MES", "MYM", "M2K", "MGC", "MCL", "M6E", "M6A", "M6B", "MJY", "MSF", "MCD", "MBT", "MET", "SIL", "MHG", "MNG")
isMicro = array.includes(MICRO_ROOTS, syminfo.root)
int qtyPerMini = isMicro ? MICROS_PER_MINI : 1
float commSide = iCommMode == COMM_AUTO ? (isMicro ? 0.25 : 0.75) : iCommCustom
float rtCost = 2.0 * commSide
float pv = syminfo.pointvalue
float tick = syminfo.mintick
float slipPx = SLIP_TICKS * tick
bool isPA = iMode == "Performance Account"
bool isRaw = iMode == MODE_RAW
int rawCap = iMaxQty > 0 ? math.min(iRawMaxMinis * qtyPerMini, iMaxQty) : iRawMaxMinis * qtyPerMini
float evalStop = iFeed == "Tradovate" ? EVAL_STOP_TRADOVATE : EVAL_STOP_RITHMIC
float planStopLevel = isPA ? PA_STOP : evalStop
bool favFirst = iOrder == ORD_FAV
bool rndStopFirst = iAmb == AMB_STOP
bool exitJuly = iExit == EXIT_JULY

// --------------------------------------------------------------- helpers ----
rNear(float p) =>
    na(p) ? na : math.round(p / syminfo.mintick) * syminfo.mintick
rDown(float p) =>
    na(p) ? na : math.floor(p / syminfo.mintick + 1e-9) * syminfo.mintick
rUp(float p) =>
    na(p) ? na : math.ceil(p / syminfo.mintick - 1e-9) * syminfo.mintick

etMinutes(int t) =>
    hour(t, TZ) * 60 + minute(t, TZ)

// Trading day of a timestamp as 00:00 UTC of its date (like time_tradingday):
// the ET date six hours later, so 18:00 ET onwards counts toward the next day.
tradingDayOf(int t) =>
    int t6 = t + 6 * 3600000
    timestamp("UTC", year(t6, TZ), month(t6, TZ), dayofmonth(t6, TZ), 0, 0)

parseHM(string s, int at) =>
    float h = str.tonumber(str.substring(s, at, at + 2))
    float m = str.tonumber(str.substring(s, at + 2, at + 4))
    na(h) or na(m) ? na : h * 60 + m

// Park-Miller minimal standard generator, reseeded each trading day from the
// day and the seed, so a given bar draws the same numbers on every run.
pmNext(int s) =>
    (s * 48271) % 2147483647
rngSeed(int dayMs, int seed) =>
    int dayNum = int(math.floor(dayMs / 86400000.0))
    int r0 = (dayNum * 7919 + math.abs(seed) * 104729) % 67108859 + 1
    int r1 = (r0 * r0) % 2147483647
    pmNext(pmNext(r1 == 0 ? 1 : r1))

// ------------------------------------------------------------- clock -------
bool newDay = bar_index == 0 or time_tradingday != time_tradingday[1]
int etMin = etMinutes(time)
int closeMin = etMinutes(time_close)
float winStart = parseHM(iWindow, 0)
float winEnd = parseHM(iWindow, 5)
float tfMin = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) / 60.0
int flatByMin = math.min(iFlatH * 60 + iFlatM, FLAT_BY_ET_MIN)
// The flat-by close is a market order filling at the next bar's open (this
// bar's close time), so it goes out on the first bar whose NEXT close would
// be after the flat-by time; entries stop before that bar.
bool atFlatBy = closeMin + tfMin > flatByMin and closeMin < 18 * 60
bool inWindow = not na(winStart) and not na(winEnd) and closeMin >= winStart and closeMin < winEnd and closeMin < flatByMin and not atFlatBy
// Out-of-sample split by the attempt's first trading day (time_tradingday is
// 00:00 UTC of the trading date) against the chosen calendar date in ET.
int oosDay = timestamp("UTC", year(iOOS, TZ), month(iOOS, TZ), dayofmonth(iOOS, TZ), 0, 0)
float minsSinceOpen = (time - timestamp(TZ, year(time, TZ), month(time, TZ), dayofmonth(time, TZ), 9, 30)) / 60000.0
bool sessDrive = etMin >= 570 and etMin < 600
bool sessMorning = etMin >= 600 and etMin < 690
bool sessLunch = etMin >= 690 and etMin < 810
bool sessPower = etMin >= 900 and etMin < 950

// --------------------------------------------- July NQ indicator stack -----
// Same EMAs, Wilder ATR/RSI/ADX, session VWAP with volume-weighted bands,
// ATR percentile, pivots, 15m bias, prior-day levels and opening range as the
// July nqcopilot engine (indicators.py / market.py).
float emaF = ta.ema(close, 9)
float emaM = ta.ema(close, 21)
float emaS = ta.ema(close, 50)
float atrV = ta.atr(14)
float rsiV = ta.rsi(close, 14)
[diPlus, diMinus, adxV] = ta.dmi(14, 14)
[vwapV, vwapU1, vwapL1] = ta.vwap(hlc3, newDay, 1.0)
float vwapSd = vwapU1 - vwapV
float atrRank = ta.percentrank(atrV, 100)
float volAvgPrev = ta.sma(volume, 20)[1]
float rvol = na(volAvgPrev) or volAvgPrev <= 0 ? na : volume / volAvgPrev
float lo4 = ta.lowest(low, 4)
float hi4 = ta.highest(high, 4)
float lo10 = ta.lowest(low, 10)
float hi10 = ta.highest(high, 10)
float belowN = math.sum(close < vwapV ? 1 : 0, 6)[1]
float aboveN = math.sum(close > vwapV ? 1 : 0, 6)[1]

// 15-minute bias from the last completed 15m bar: close vs EMA21 with the
// EMA's 5-point least-squares slope agreeing (market.py _bias_from).
// lookahead_on with [1] gives the same completed bar historically and live.
htfBiasCalc() =>
    float e = ta.ema(close, 21)
    float slope = (2.0 * (e - e[4]) + (e[1] - e[3])) / 10.0
    int b = 0
    if not na(e)
        if close > e and (na(slope) or slope >= 0)
            b := 1
        else if close < e and (na(slope) or slope <= 0)
            b := -1
    b
int htfBiasRaw = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "15", htfBiasCalc()[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
int htfBias = nz(htfBiasRaw, 0)

// Prior trading day's high/low, computed on the chart (no request.security).
var float dayHi = na
var float dayLo = na
var float pdHigh = na
var float pdLow = na
if newDay
    if not na(dayHi)
        pdHigh := dayHi
        pdLow := dayLo
    dayHi := high
    dayLo := low
else
    dayHi := math.max(dayHi, high)
    dayLo := math.min(dayLo, low)

// Confirmed swing pivots (3 left / 3 right, ties allowed), published 3 bars late.
bool isPH = bar_index >= 6 and high <= high[3] and high[1] <= high[3] and high[2] <= high[3] and high[4] <= high[3] and high[5] <= high[3] and high[6] <= high[3]
bool isPL = bar_index >= 6 and low >= low[3] and low[1] >= low[3] and low[2] >= low[3] and low[4] >= low[3] and low[5] >= low[3] and low[6] >= low[3]
var float lastPH = na
var float lastPL = na
if isPH
    lastPH := high[3]
if isPL
    lastPL := low[3]

// Opening range 09:30-10:00 ET, complete once a bar opens at or after 10:00.
var float orHi = na
var float orLo = na
var bool orDone = false
if newDay
    orHi := na
    orLo := na
    orDone := false
if etMin >= 570 and etMin < 600
    orHi := na(orHi) ? high : math.max(orHi, high)
    orLo := na(orLo) ? low : math.min(orLo, low)
else if etMin >= 600 and not na(orHi)
    orDone := true

int emaStack = na(emaF) or na(emaM) or na(emaS) ? 0 : emaF > emaM and emaM > emaS ? 1 : emaF < emaM and emaM < emaS ? -1 : 0
int regime = not na(atrRank) and atrRank >= 90 ? REG_EXP : not na(atrRank) and atrRank <= 15 ? REG_QUIET : na(adxV) or na(diPlus) or na(diMinus) ? REG_CHOP : adxV >= 23 and diPlus > diMinus and emaStack >= 0 ? REG_UP : adxV >= 23 and diMinus > diPlus and emaStack <= 0 ? REG_DOWN : REG_CHOP
bool isRange = regime == REG_CHOP or regime == REG_QUIET
float closePos = high - low <= 0 ? 0.5 : (close - low) / (high - low)
bool warm = bar_index >= WARMUP_BARS and not na(emaS) and not na(atrV) and not na(adxV) and not na(vwapV) and not na(atrRank)

// Context support for a direction (signals.py _confluence).
confluence(int dir) =>
    float pts = 0.0
    pts += htfBias == dir ? 15 : htfBias == -dir ? -12 : 0
    pts += emaStack == dir ? 10 : emaStack == -dir ? -8 : 0
    if not na(vwapV)
        pts += (dir > 0 ? close > vwapV : close < vwapV) ? 10 : -6
    if not na(adxV)
        pts += math.max(0.0, math.min(15.0, (adxV - 15.0) * 0.9))
    if not na(rvol)
        pts += rvol >= 1.3 ? 10 : rvol < 0.7 ? -8 : 0
    pts += sessDrive or sessMorning ? 10 : sessLunch ? -15 : sessPower ? 5 : 0
    if not na(rsiV)
        pts += dir > 0 and rsiV > 78 ? -10 : dir < 0 and rsiV < 22 ? -10 : 0
    pts
float scoreL = confluence(1)
float scoreS = confluence(-1)

// Snap to ticks (stops and targets rounded the conservative way) and reject
// broken geometry (signals.py _build_setup).
buildSetup(int dir, float entryRaw, float stopRaw, float t1Raw, float t2Raw, float scoreRaw) =>
    float e = rNear(entryRaw)
    float s = dir > 0 ? rDown(stopRaw) : rUp(stopRaw)
    float a = dir > 0 ? rDown(t1Raw) : rUp(t1Raw)
    float b = dir > 0 ? rDown(t2Raw) : rUp(t2Raw)
    bool okNum = dir != 0 and not na(e) and not na(s) and not na(a) and not na(b) and not na(scoreRaw)
    bool okGeo = okNum and (dir > 0 ? s < e and e < a and a <= b : s > e and e > a and a >= b) and math.abs(e - s) >= syminfo.mintick
    [okGeo, e, s, a, b, math.max(0.0, math.min(100.0, nz(scoreRaw)))]

float stopStructL = (na(lastPL) ? lo10 : math.min(lastPL, lo10)) - 0.25 * atrV
float stopStructS = (na(lastPH) ? hi10 : math.max(lastPH, hi10)) + 0.25 * atrV

// 1. Trend Pullback (detect_trend_pullback)
int tpDir0 = regime == REG_UP ? 1 : regime == REG_DOWN ? -1 : 0
float refHi = na(vwapV) ? emaM : math.max(emaM, vwapV)
float refLo = na(vwapV) ? emaM : math.min(emaM, vwapV)
bool tpLong = tpDir0 == 1 and lo4 <= refHi + 0.35 * atrV and close > open and closePos >= 0.6 and close > emaM
bool tpShort = tpDir0 == -1 and hi4 >= refLo - 0.35 * atrV and close <= open and closePos <= 0.4 and close < emaM
int tpDir = not na(emaM) and (tpLong or tpShort) ? tpDir0 : 0
float tpStop = tpDir > 0 ? stopStructL : stopStructS
float tpRisk = math.abs(close - tpStop)
[tpOk, tpE, tpS, tpA, tpB, tpSc] = buildSetup(tpDir, close, tpStop, close + tpRisk * 1.5 * tpDir, close + tpRisk * 3.0 * tpDir, (tpDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 22)

// 2. Opening Range Breakout (detect_orb_breakout)
float orW = orHi - orLo
bool orbGate = orDone and not na(orHi) and not na(orLo) and minsSinceOpen >= 30 and minsSinceOpen <= 180 and orW <= 3.0 * atrV and orW >= 0.4 * atrV and not isRange
int orbRaw = close > orHi and close[1] <= orHi ? 1 : close < orLo and close[1] >= orLo ? -1 : 0
bool orbBar = orbRaw == 1 ? closePos >= 0.55 : orbRaw == -1 ? closePos <= 0.45 : false
int orbDir = orbGate and orbBar ? orbRaw : 0
float orbStop = orbDir > 0 ? math.min(stopStructL, orHi - 0.3 * atrV) : math.max(stopStructS, orLo + 0.3 * atrV)
float orbRisk = math.abs(close - orbStop)
[orbOk, orbE, orbS, orbA, orbB, orbSc] = buildSetup(orbDir, close, orbStop, close + orbRisk * 1.5 * orbDir, close + math.max(orbRisk * 2.5, orW) * orbDir, (orbDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 25)

// 3. VWAP Reclaim (detect_vwap_reclaim)
bool vrGate = bar_index >= 6 and not na(vwapV) and not na(vwapV[6]) and regime != REG_EXP
int vrRaw = belowN >= 4 and close > vwapV and close > open ? 1 : aboveN >= 4 and close < vwapV and close <= open ? -1 : 0
int vrDir = vrGate ? vrRaw : 0
float vrStop = vrDir > 0 ? math.min(stopStructL, vwapV - 0.4 * atrV) : math.max(stopStructS, vwapV + 0.4 * atrV)
float vrRisk = math.abs(close - vrStop)
[vrOk, vrE, vrS, vrA, vrB, vrSc] = buildSetup(vrDir, close, vrStop, close + vrRisk * 1.5 * vrDir, close + vrRisk * 2.5 * vrDir, (vrDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 15)

// 4. Failed Breakout Reversal (detect_failed_breakout)
int fbRaw = not na(pdHigh) and hi4 > pdHigh and close < pdHigh ? -1 : not na(pdLow) and lo4 < pdLow and close > pdLow ? 1 : 0
float fbLevel = fbRaw < 0 ? hi4 : lo4
float fbRef = fbRaw < 0 ? pdHigh : pdLow
bool fbValid = bar_index >= 3 and fbRaw != 0 and math.abs(fbLevel - fbRef) >= 0.15 * atrV and (fbRaw > 0 ? close > open : close <= open)
int fbDir = fbValid ? fbRaw : 0
float fbStop = fbDir < 0 ? fbLevel + 0.3 * atrV : fbLevel - 0.3 * atrV
float fbRisk = math.abs(close - fbStop)
float fbT2 = not na(vwapV) and (vwapV - close) * fbDir > fbRisk * 2 ? vwapV : close + fbRisk * 2.5 * fbDir
[fbOk, fbE, fbS, fbA, fbB, fbSc] = buildSetup(fbDir, close, fbStop, close + fbRisk * 1.5 * fbDir, fbT2, (fbDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 18)

// 5. VWAP Fade (detect_vwap_fade), range regimes only
float sigma = not na(vwapSd) and vwapSd > 0 ? (close - vwapV) / vwapSd : na
int fadeRaw = isRange and not na(sigma) and math.abs(sigma) >= 2.0 ? (sigma > 0 ? -1 : 1) : 0
float bodyAbs = math.abs(close - open)
bool fadeShortOk = (high - math.max(open, close) > bodyAbs * 0.8 or close <= open) and (na(rsiV) or rsiV > 62)
bool fadeLongOk = (math.min(open, close) - low > bodyAbs * 0.8 or close > open) and (na(rsiV) or rsiV < 38)
int fadeDir = fadeRaw < 0 and fadeShortOk ? -1 : fadeRaw > 0 and fadeLongOk ? 1 : 0
float fadeStop = fadeDir < 0 ? high + 0.5 * atrV : low - 0.5 * atrV
float fadeRisk = math.abs(close - fadeStop)
float fadeT1 = close + math.min(math.abs(close - vwapV) * 0.6, fadeRisk * 1.5) * fadeDir
[fadeOk, fadeE, fadeS, fadeA, fadeB, fadeSc] = buildSetup(fadeRisk > 0 ? fadeDir : 0, close, fadeStop, fadeT1, vwapV, (fadeDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 12)

// Best enabled candidate by score; ties keep detector order (detect_all).
int jDir = 0
float jE = na
float jS = na
float jA = na
float jB = na
float jSc = -1.0
if iUseTP and tpOk and tpSc > jSc
    jDir := tpDir
    jE := tpE
    jS := tpS
    jA := tpA
    jB := tpB
    jSc := tpSc
if iUseORB and orbOk and orbSc > jSc
    jDir := orbDir
    jE := orbE
    jS := orbS
    jA := orbA
    jB := orbB
    jSc := orbSc
if iUseVR and vrOk and vrSc > jSc
    jDir := vrDir
    jE := vrE
    jS := vrS
    jA := vrA
    jB := vrB
    jSc := vrSc
if iUseFB and fbOk and fbSc > jSc
    jDir := fbDir
    jE := fbE
    jS := fbS
    jA := fbA
    jB := fbB
    jSc := fbSc
if iUseFade and fadeOk and fadeSc > jSc
    jDir := fadeDir
    jE := fadeE
    jS := fadeS
    jA := fadeA
    jB := fadeB
    jSc := fadeSc
// July playbook gates on the best candidate only: score, stop sanity, net R.
float jStopPts = math.abs(jE - jS)
float jNetR = (math.abs(jA - jE) * pv - rtCost) / (jStopPts * pv + rtCost)
bool julyPass = jDir != 0 and jSc >= iMinScore and jStopPts >= iMinStop and jStopPts <= iMaxStop and jNetR >= iMinNetR

// ------------------------------------------------------------ random draws --
var int rngState = 1
if newDay
    rngState := rngSeed(time_tradingday, iSeed)
rngState := pmNext(rngState)
float u1 = rngState / 2147483647.0
rngState := pmNext(rngState)
float u2 = rngState / 2147483647.0

// ======================================================== APEX LEDGER =======
// One type, one set of methods, used by both the signal ledger (fills from
// strategy.*) and the random-control ledger (fills simulated in plain Pine).
type Ledger
    int status = 0
    float realized = 0.0
    float peak = 50000.0
    float threshold = 48000.0
    float dd = 2000.0
    float stopLevel = na
    bool pa = false
    int startTime = 0
    int startDay = 0
    bool oos = false
    int tradedDays = 0
    int lastTradeDay = 0
    int sessions = 0
    float dayStartBal = 50000.0
    int tier = 1
    bool dllHit = false
    int dayEvent = 0
    array<int> nStarted
    array<int> nPassed
    array<int> nBreached
    array<int> nExpired
    array<float> daysIS
    array<float> daysOOS
    int ambiguous = 0
    int skippedSize = 0
    int entries = 0

newLedger() =>
    Ledger.new(nStarted = array.new<int>(2, 0), nPassed = array.new<int>(2, 0), nBreached = array.new<int>(2, 0), nExpired = array.new<int>(2, 0), daysIS = array.new<float>(), daysOOS = array.new<float>())

method bal(Ledger L) =>
    START_BAL + L.realized

method active(Ledger L) =>
    L.status == ST_ACTIVE

method begin(Ledger L, bool pa, float stopLevel, int oosFrom) =>
    L.status := ST_ACTIVE
    L.realized := 0.0
    L.peak := START_BAL
    L.dd := pa ? PA_DD : EVAL_DD
    L.threshold := START_BAL - L.dd
    L.stopLevel := stopLevel
    L.pa := pa
    L.startTime := time
    L.startDay := time_tradingday
    L.oos := time_tradingday >= oosFrom
    L.tradedDays := 0
    L.lastTradeDay := 0
    L.sessions := 1
    L.dayStartBal := START_BAL
    L.tier := 1
    L.dllHit := false
    int si = L.oos ? 1 : 0
    L.nStarted.set(si, L.nStarted.get(si) + 1)

// Close the attempt with a terminal status and record it.
method finish(Ledger L, int st) =>
    if L.status == ST_ACTIVE
        L.status := st
        L.dayEvent := st
        int si = L.oos ? 1 : 0
        bool recordDays = (st == ST_PASSED and not L.pa) or (st == ST_BREACHED and L.pa)
        if st == ST_PASSED
            L.nPassed.set(si, L.nPassed.get(si) + 1)
        else if st == ST_BREACHED
            L.nBreached.set(si, L.nBreached.get(si) + 1)
        else if st == ST_EXPIRED
            L.nExpired.set(si, L.nExpired.get(si) + 1)
        if recordDays
            if L.oos
                L.daysOOS.push(L.tradedDays)
            else
                L.daysIS.push(L.tradedDays)

// observe(b): raise peak/threshold on a new high, then breach on a touch.
method observe(Ledger L, float b) =>
    if L.status == ST_ACTIVE and not na(b)
        if b > L.peak
            L.peak := b
            float trail = L.peak - L.dd
            float capped = na(L.stopLevel) ? trail : math.min(trail, L.stopLevel)
            L.threshold := math.max(L.threshold, capped)
        if b <= L.threshold
            L.finish(ST_BREACHED)

// One bar: b0 is the balance at the bar's start, m1/m2 open-P&L marks already
// in observation order (see barMarks), bClose the balance at the close.
method observeBar(Ledger L, float b0, float m1, float m2, float bClose) =>
    if not na(m1)
        L.observe(b0 + m1)
    if not na(m2)
        L.observe(b0 + m2)
    L.observe(bClose)

// New trading session: tier from the prior session's closing balance, DLL
// reset, the 30-calendar-day evaluation access window, and the PA horizon
// (a PA that survived iPaHorizon sessions ends as ST_EXPIRED = survived).
method dayRoll(Ledger L) =>
    if L.status == ST_ACTIVE
        float closeBal = L.bal()
        L.dayStartBal := closeBal
        L.dllHit := false
        if L.pa
            if L.sessions >= iPaHorizon
                L.finish(ST_EXPIRED)
            else
                L.sessions += 1
                float prof = closeBal - START_BAL
                L.tier := prof >= PA_T4_PROFIT ? 4 : prof >= PA_T3_PROFIT ? 3 : prof >= PA_T2_PROFIT ? 2 : 1
        else if time_tradingday - L.startDay >= EVAL_ACCESS_DAYS * DAY_MS
            L.finish(ST_EXPIRED)
    L.status

// Daily loss limit on the session's worst observed balance: the PA tier's,
// or EVAL_DLL in the evaluation (na = none).
method dllCheck(Ledger L, float worstBal) =>
    bool hit = false
    float dll = L.pa ? (L.tier == 4 ? PA_T4_DLL : L.tier == 3 ? PA_T3_DLL : L.tier == 2 ? PA_T2_DLL : PA_T1_DLL) : EVAL_DLL
    if L.status == ST_ACTIVE and not L.dllHit and not na(worstBal) and not na(dll)
        if worstBal - L.dayStartBal <= -dll
            L.dllHit := true
            hit := true
    hit

// Evaluation pass: flat, closed P&L at or above the target.
method passCheck(Ledger L) =>
    if L.status == ST_ACTIVE and not L.pa and L.realized >= EVAL_TARGET
        L.finish(ST_PASSED)

method planCap(Ledger L, int perMini, int override) =>
    int minis = L.pa ? (L.tier == 4 ? PA_T4_MINIS : L.tier == 3 ? PA_T3_MINIS : L.tier == 2 ? PA_T2_MINIS : PA_T1_MINIS) : EVAL_MAX_MINIS
    int cap = minis * perMini
    override > 0 ? math.min(cap, override) : cap

method noteEntry(Ledger L) =>
    L.entries += 1
    if time_tradingday != L.lastTradeDay
        L.tradedDays += 1
        L.lastTradeDay := time_tradingday

// qty = floor(risk$ / (stop points x point value + round-trip cost)), capped.
sizeFor(float stopPts, float riskUsd, int cap, float pointValue, float roundTrip) =>
    float perC = stopPts * pointValue + roundTrip
    na(perC) or perC <= 0 ? 0 : math.min(cap, int(math.floor(riskUsd / perC)))

// ======================================================= RAW TRADE STATS ====
// Raw trades mode only: per-trade results, [0] in-sample, [1] out-of-sample.
type RawStats
    array<int> n
    array<int> wins
    array<float> net
    array<float> grossWin
    array<float> grossLoss
    array<float> perContract

newRawStats() =>
    RawStats.new(n = array.new<int>(2, 0), wins = array.new<int>(2, 0), net = array.new<float>(2, 0.0), grossWin = array.new<float>(2, 0.0), grossLoss = array.new<float>(2, 0.0), perContract = array.new<float>(2, 0.0))

// One finished trade: net P&L in dollars as traded, contracts at entry.
method add(RawStats S, bool oos, float pnl, float qty) =>
    int si = oos ? 1 : 0
    S.n.set(si, S.n.get(si) + 1)
    S.net.set(si, S.net.get(si) + pnl)
    if pnl > 0
        S.wins.set(si, S.wins.get(si) + 1)
        S.grossWin.set(si, S.grossWin.get(si) + pnl)
    else if pnl < 0
        S.grossLoss.set(si, S.grossLoss.get(si) - pnl)
    if qty > 0
        S.perContract.set(si, S.perContract.get(si) + pnl / qty)

// ============================================================ POSITION ======
type Pos
    int dir = 0
    float qty0 = 0.0
    float qty = 0.0
    float qtyT1 = 0.0
    float entry = na
    float stop = na
    float stop0 = na
    float t1 = na
    float tgt = na
    bool t1Done = false
    bool beDone = false
    string eid = ""
    int pDir = 0
    float pQty = 0.0
    float pQtyT1 = 0.0
    float pStop = na
    float pT1 = na
    float pTgt = na
    bool pFlat = false

method openFromPending(Pos p, float fillPx) =>
    p.dir := p.pDir
    p.qty0 := p.pQty
    p.qty := p.pQty
    p.qtyT1 := p.pQtyT1
    p.entry := fillPx
    p.stop := p.pStop
    p.stop0 := p.pStop
    p.t1 := p.pT1
    p.tgt := p.pTgt
    p.t1Done := false
    p.beDone := false
    p.pDir := 0

method flatten(Pos p) =>
    p.dir := 0
    p.qty := 0.0

// Gross open P&L marks for one bar, limited to what the position could see
// while its stop and targets were working, returned in observation order.
// Also reports whether the bar touched both the stop and a target.
barMarks(Pos p, bool favorableFirst, float slip, float pointValue) =>
    float d = p.dir
    float eF = d * p.entry
    float oF = d * open
    float hiF = d > 0 ? high : -low
    float loF = d > 0 ? low : -high
    float sF = d * p.stop
    float tgF = d * p.tgt
    bool t1P = p.qtyT1 > 0 and not p.t1Done
    float t1F = t1P ? d * p.t1 : na
    float q = p.qty
    float qT1 = t1P ? p.qtyT1 : 0.0
    float mFirst = na
    float mSecond = na
    bool amb = false
    if oF <= sF
        mFirst := q * (oF - slip - eF) * pointValue
        mSecond := mFirst
    else if oF >= tgF
        mFirst := q * (oF - eF) * pointValue
        mSecond := mFirst
    else
        bool stopHit = loF <= sF
        bool t1Hit = t1P and hiF >= t1F
        bool tgtHit = hiF >= tgF
        amb := stopHit and (t1Hit or tgtHit)
        float favPx = math.min(hiF, tgF)
        float advPx = stopHit ? sF - slip : loF
        float realT1 = t1Hit ? qT1 * (math.max(oF, t1F) - eF) * pointValue : 0.0
        float favPnl = t1Hit ? realT1 + (q - qT1) * (favPx - eF) * pointValue : q * (favPx - eF) * pointValue
        if favorableFirst
            float rem = tgtHit ? 0.0 : t1Hit ? q - qT1 : q
            mFirst := favPnl
            mSecond := tgtHit ? favPnl : realT1 + rem * (advPx - eF) * pointValue
        else
            // A T1 limit the open gapped through filled at the open (as in
            // simExits), so that leg cannot reach the low or the stop.
            bool t1Gap = t1P and oF >= t1F
            float advPnl = t1Gap ? realT1 + (q - qT1) * (advPx - eF) * pointValue : q * (advPx - eF) * pointValue
            mFirst := advPnl
            mSecond := stopHit ? advPnl : favPnl
    [mFirst, mSecond, amb]

// Shadow fills for one bar: gaps fill at the open, then either stop-first or
// TradingView's OHLC path decides a bar that touches both sides.
// Returns [gross P&L closed, contracts closed].
simExits(Pos p, bool stopFirst, float slip, float pointValue) =>
    float d = p.dir
    float eF = d * p.entry
    float oF = d * open
    float hiF = d > 0 ? high : -low
    float loF = d > 0 ? low : -high
    float sF = d * p.stop
    float tgF = d * p.tgt
    bool t1P = p.qtyT1 > 0 and not p.t1Done
    float t1F = t1P ? d * p.t1 : na
    float gross = 0.0
    float closed = 0.0
    float q = p.qty
    if oF <= sF
        gross := q * (oF - slip - eF) * pointValue
        closed := q
        q := 0.0
    else if oF >= tgF
        gross := q * (oF - eF) * pointValue
        closed := q
        q := 0.0
    else
        bool t1Now = false
        if t1P and oF >= t1F
            gross += p.qtyT1 * (oF - eF) * pointValue
            closed += p.qtyT1
            q -= p.qtyT1
            t1Now := true
        bool stopHit = loF <= sF
        bool t1Hit = t1P and not t1Now and hiF >= t1F
        bool tgtHit = hiF >= tgF
        bool highFirst = high - open < open - low
        bool favPath = stopFirst ? false : d > 0 ? highFirst : not highFirst
        if favPath
            if t1Hit
                gross += p.qtyT1 * (t1F - eF) * pointValue
                closed += p.qtyT1
                q -= p.qtyT1
                t1Now := true
            if tgtHit
                gross += q * (tgF - eF) * pointValue
                closed += q
                q := 0.0
            else if stopHit
                gross += q * (sF - slip - eF) * pointValue
                closed += q
                q := 0.0
        else
            if stopHit
                gross += q * (sF - slip - eF) * pointValue
                closed += q
                q := 0.0
            else
                if t1Hit
                    gross += p.qtyT1 * (t1F - eF) * pointValue
                    closed += p.qtyT1
                    q -= p.qtyT1
                    t1Now := true
                if tgtHit
                    gross += q * (tgF - eF) * pointValue
                    closed += q
                    q := 0.0
        if t1Now
            p.t1Done := true
    p.qty := q
    if q <= 0
        p.dir := 0
    [gross, closed]

// Stop to breakeven once the position has touched +1R (July playbook).
method breakeven(Pos p) =>
    if p.dir != 0 and not p.beDone
        float oneR = p.entry + p.dir * math.abs(p.entry - p.stop0)
        if p.dir > 0 ? high >= oneR : low <= oneR
            p.stop := p.entry
            p.beDone := true

// Pending entry: stop and targets from the signal bar's close.
method arm(Pos p, int dir, float qty, float entryEst, float stopPx, float t1Px, float t2Px) =>
    float risk = math.abs(entryEst - stopPx)
    p.pDir := dir
    p.pQty := qty
    p.pStop := stopPx
    if exitJuly
        float a = na(t1Px) ? (dir > 0 ? rDown(entryEst + 1.5 * risk) : rUp(entryEst - 1.5 * risk)) : t1Px
        float b = na(t2Px) ? (dir > 0 ? rDown(entryEst + 2.5 * risk) : rUp(entryEst - 2.5 * risk)) : t2Px
        p.pT1 := a
        p.pQtyT1 := qty >= 2 ? math.floor(qty / 2) : 0.0
        p.pTgt := qty >= 2 ? b : a
    else
        p.pT1 := na
        p.pQtyT1 := 0.0
        p.pTgt := dir > 0 ? rDown(entryEst + iRMult * risk) : rUp(entryEst - iRMult * risk)

var Ledger sigL = newLedger()
var Ledger rndL = newLedger()
var Pos sp = Pos.new()
var Pos rp = Pos.new()
var RawStats sigRaw = newRawStats()
var RawStats rndRaw = newRawStats()
sigL.dayEvent := 0
rndL.dayEvent := 0

// ===================================================== SIGNAL LEDGER =======
// Fills come from the strategy.* broker emulator; the ledger reads them back.
var float npAtStart = 0.0
var float paidComm = 0.0
var float labCost = 0.0
var float paidAtStart = 0.0
var float labAtStart = 0.0
var int prevClosed = 0
var int tradeNo = 0
// Raw trades mode: the position whose exit legs are being summed.
var string rawSId = ""
var bool rawSOos = false
var float rawSPnl = 0.0
var float rawSQty = 0.0

// Read back every trade the emulator closed since the last bar. A trade that
// exited at an earlier bar's close (strategy.close_all(immediately = true))
// belongs to that bar, so it is booked before this bar's day roll and marks.
float bookedNow = 0.0
int closedBefore = prevClosed
int nowClosed = strategy.closedtrades
if nowClosed > prevClosed
    for i = prevClosed to nowClosed - 1
        float tradeComm = strategy.closedtrades.commission(i)
        float tradeLab = rtCost * math.abs(strategy.closedtrades.size(i))
        paidComm += tradeComm
        labCost += tradeLab
        if strategy.closedtrades.exit_bar_index(i) >= bar_index
            bookedNow += strategy.closedtrades.profit(i) + tradeComm - tradeLab
        if isRaw
            // Each exit leg is its own closed trade; legs of one entry share
            // its id. Lab costs replace the Properties-tab commission.
            string legId = strategy.closedtrades.entry_id(i)
            if legId != rawSId and rawSQty > 0
                sigRaw.add(rawSOos, rawSPnl, rawSQty)
                rawSPnl := 0.0
                rawSQty := 0.0
            rawSId := legId
            rawSOos := tradingDayOf(strategy.closedtrades.entry_time(i)) >= oosDay
            rawSPnl += strategy.closedtrades.profit(i) + tradeComm - tradeLab
            rawSQty += math.abs(strategy.closedtrades.size(i))
    prevClosed := nowClosed
// Raw trades mode: a position is finished once the emulator is flat.
if isRaw and rawSQty > 0 and strategy.position_size == 0
    sigRaw.add(rawSOos, rawSPnl, rawSQty)
    rawSPnl := 0.0
    rawSQty := 0.0
// realized = strategy.netprofit - netprofit at attempt start, with the
// Properties-tab commission swapped for the lab's cost model.
float sRealizedNow = (strategy.netprofit - npAtStart) + (paidComm - paidAtStart) - (labCost - labAtStart)
if sigL.active()
    sigL.realized := sRealizedNow - bookedNow

if newDay
    // A session-end close_all(immediately = true) is read back on this bar.
    // Settle the breach or pass it caused before the day roll, so it belongs
    // to the session that produced it (as in the random ledger), the access
    // window cannot expire it first, and the next attempt can start now.
    if strategy.position_size == 0 and sp.dir == 0 and sp.pDir == 0 and not sp.pFlat
        sigL.observe(sigL.bal())
        sigL.passCheck()
    sigL.dayRoll()
    if not isRaw and not sigL.active() and warm and strategy.position_size == 0 and sp.dir == 0 and sp.pDir == 0 and not sp.pFlat
        sigL.begin(isPA, planStopLevel, oosDay)
        npAtStart := strategy.netprofit
        paidAtStart := paidComm
        labAtStart := labCost
        sRealizedNow := 0.0

float sB0 = sigL.bal()
float sM1 = na
float sM2 = na
if sp.pFlat and sp.dir != 0
    sM1 := sp.qty * (sp.dir * (open - sp.entry) - slipPx) * pv
    sM2 := sM1
    sp.flatten()
sp.pFlat := false
if sp.pDir != 0
    float fillPx = strategy.position_size != 0 ? strategy.position_avg_price : nowClosed > closedBefore ? strategy.closedtrades.entry_price(nowClosed - 1) : na
    if na(fillPx)
        sp.pDir := 0
    else
        sp.openFromPending(fillPx)
        if sigL.active()
            sigL.noteEntry()
if sp.dir != 0 and na(sM1)
    [mA, mB, mAmb] = barMarks(sp, favFirst, slipPx, pv)
    sM1 := mA
    sM2 := mB
    if mAmb and (isRaw or sigL.active())
        sigL.ambiguous += 1

// Sync with the broker emulator: this bar's exits, then the position left.
if sigL.active()
    sigL.realized := sRealizedNow
float posSize = strategy.position_size
if posSize == 0
    sp.flatten()
else
    sp.qty := math.abs(posSize)
    if sp.qtyT1 > 0 and sp.qty <= sp.qty0 - sp.qtyT1
        sp.t1Done := true
float sOpenClose = posSize != 0 ? (close - strategy.position_avg_price) * posSize * pv : 0.0
float sBClose = sigL.bal() + sOpenClose
sigL.observeBar(sB0, sM1, sM2, sBClose)
float sWorst = math.min(na(sM1) ? sBClose : sB0 + math.min(sM1, sM2), sBClose)
bool sDll = sigL.dllCheck(sWorst)
if posSize == 0 and sp.pDir == 0
    sigL.passCheck()
if exitJuly
    sp.breakeven()

// Decide what the strategy does at this close.
bool sHasPos = posSize != 0
bool sNow = sHasPos and (session.islastbar or (newDay and bar_index > 0))
// Raw trades mode has no attempt to end and no DLL (the ledger never starts).
bool sFlat = sHasPos and not sNow and ((not isRaw and not sigL.active()) or sDll or atFlatBy or sp.dir == 0)
bool sElig = warm and (isRaw or sigL.active()) and not sHasPos and sp.pDir == 0 and inWindow and not sigL.dllHit and not session.islastbar

int sigDir = 0
float sigE = na
float sigStop = na
float sigT1 = na
float sigT2 = na
if sElig
    if iSource == SRC_JULY
        if julyPass
            sigDir := jDir
            sigE := jE
            sigStop := jS
            sigT1 := jA
            sigT2 := jB
    else if iSource == SRC_EXT
        int xd = iExtSrc > 0 ? 1 : iExtSrc < 0 ? -1 : 0
        if xd != 0 and not na(atrV)
            sigDir := xd
            sigE := rNear(close)
            sigStop := xd > 0 ? rDown(close - iExtAtr * atrV) : rUp(close + iExtAtr * atrV)
    else
        if u1 < iRndProb and not na(atrV)
            sigDir := u2 < 0.5 ? 1 : -1
            sigE := rNear(close)
            sigStop := sigDir > 0 ? rDown(close - iRndAtr * atrV) : rUp(close + iRndAtr * atrV)
int sQty = 0
if sigDir != 0 and math.abs(sigE - sigStop) < tick
    sigDir := 0
if sigDir != 0
    sQty := sizeFor(math.abs(sigE - sigStop), iRisk, isRaw ? rawCap : sigL.planCap(qtyPerMini, iMaxQty), pv, rtCost)
    if sQty < 1
        sigL.skippedSize += 1
        sigDir := 0

if sNow
    strategy.close_all(comment = "session end", immediately = true)
    sp.flatten()
else if sFlat
    strategy.close_all(comment = not isRaw and not sigL.active() ? "attempt over" : sDll ? "DLL" : "flat-by")
    sp.pFlat := true
else if sHasPos
    if sp.qtyT1 > 0
        if not sp.t1Done
            strategy.exit("t1" + sp.eid, sp.eid, qty = sp.qtyT1, stop = sp.stop, limit = sp.t1)
        strategy.exit("t2" + sp.eid, sp.eid, qty = sp.qty0 - sp.qtyT1, stop = sp.stop, limit = sp.tgt)
    else
        strategy.exit("x" + sp.eid, sp.eid, stop = sp.stop, limit = sp.tgt)

if sigDir != 0
    tradeNo += 1
    sp.arm(sigDir, sQty, sigE, sigStop, sigT1, sigT2)
    sp.eid := (sigDir > 0 ? "L" : "S") + str.tostring(tradeNo)
    strategy.entry(sp.eid, sigDir > 0 ? strategy.long : strategy.short, qty = sQty)
    if sp.pQtyT1 > 0
        strategy.exit("t1" + sp.eid, sp.eid, qty = sp.pQtyT1, stop = sp.pStop, limit = sp.pT1)
        strategy.exit("t2" + sp.eid, sp.eid, qty = sp.pQty - sp.pQtyT1, stop = sp.pStop, limit = sp.pTgt)
    else
        strategy.exit("x" + sp.eid, sp.eid, stop = sp.pStop, limit = sp.pTgt)

// ===================================================== RANDOM CONTROL ======
// No strategy.* calls: same window, sizing, costs, exits and ledger rules,
// with next-bar-open fills simulated here.
// Raw trades mode: the open position's net P&L so far and its sample.
var float rRawPnl = 0.0
var bool rRawOos = false
if newDay
    rndL.dayRoll()
    if not isRaw and not rndL.active() and warm and rp.dir == 0 and rp.pDir == 0 and not rp.pFlat
        rndL.begin(isPA, planStopLevel, oosDay)

float rB0 = rndL.bal()
float rM1 = na
float rM2 = na
float rGross = 0.0
float rClosed = 0.0
if rp.pFlat and rp.dir != 0
    rM1 := rp.qty * (rp.dir * (open - rp.entry) - slipPx) * pv
    rM2 := rM1
    rGross += rM1
    rClosed += rp.qty
    rp.flatten()
rp.pFlat := false
if rp.pDir != 0
    rp.openFromPending(open + rp.pDir * slipPx)
    if rndL.active()
        rndL.noteEntry()
    if isRaw
        rRawPnl := 0.0
        rRawOos := tradingDayOf(time) >= oosDay
if rp.dir != 0 and na(rM1)
    [qA, qB, qAmb] = barMarks(rp, favFirst, slipPx, pv)
    rM1 := qA
    rM2 := qB
    if qAmb and (isRaw or rndL.active())
        rndL.ambiguous += 1
    [xg, xq] = simExits(rp, rndStopFirst, slipPx, pv)
    rGross += xg
    rClosed += xq
if rndL.active()
    rndL.realized += rGross - rClosed * rtCost
if isRaw and rClosed > 0
    rRawPnl += rGross - rClosed * rtCost
    if rp.dir == 0
        rndRaw.add(rRawOos, rRawPnl, rp.qty0)
float rOpenClose = rp.dir != 0 ? rp.qty * rp.dir * (close - rp.entry) * pv : 0.0
float rBClose = rndL.bal() + rOpenClose
rndL.observeBar(rB0, rM1, rM2, rBClose)
float rWorst = math.min(na(rM1) ? rBClose : rB0 + math.min(rM1, rM2), rBClose)
bool rDll = rndL.dllCheck(rWorst)
if exitJuly
    rp.breakeven()

bool rHasPos = rp.dir != 0
bool rNow = rHasPos and (session.islastbar or (newDay and bar_index > 0))
bool rFlat = rHasPos and not rNow and ((not isRaw and not rndL.active()) or rDll or atFlatBy)
if rNow
    float exitPx = close - rp.dir * slipPx
    if rndL.active()
        rndL.realized += rp.qty * rp.dir * (exitPx - rp.entry) * pv - rp.qty * rtCost
        rndL.observe(rndL.bal())
    if isRaw
        rndRaw.add(rRawOos, rRawPnl + rp.qty * rp.dir * (exitPx - rp.entry) * pv - rp.qty * rtCost, rp.qty0)
    rp.flatten()
else if rFlat
    rp.pFlat := true
if rp.dir == 0 and rp.pDir == 0
    rndL.passCheck()

bool rElig = warm and (isRaw or rndL.active()) and rp.dir == 0 and rp.pDir == 0 and not rp.pFlat and inWindow and not rndL.dllHit and not session.islastbar
if rElig and u1 < iRndProb and not na(atrV)
    int rd = u2 < 0.5 ? 1 : -1
    float re = rNear(close)
    float rs = rd > 0 ? rDown(close - iRndAtr * atrV) : rUp(close + iRndAtr * atrV)
    int rq = math.abs(re - rs) < tick ? 0 : sizeFor(math.abs(re - rs), iRisk, isRaw ? rawCap : rndL.planCap(qtyPerMini, iMaxQty), pv, rtCost)
    if rq >= 1
        rp.arm(rd, rq, re, rs, na, na)
    else
        rndL.skippedSize += 1

// ============================================================ DISPLAY ======
plotchar(sigL.dayEvent == ST_PASSED, "Signal attempt passed", "P", location.top, color.new(color.teal, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotchar(sigL.dayEvent == ST_BREACHED, "Signal attempt breached", "B", location.top, color.new(color.red, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotchar(sigL.dayEvent == ST_EXPIRED, "Signal attempt expired (PA: survived horizon)", "E", location.top, color.new(color.gray, 0), size = size.tiny)

statusText(int st) =>
    st == ST_ACTIVE ? "ACTIVE" : st == ST_PASSED ? "PASSED" : st == ST_BREACHED ? "BREACHED" : st == ST_EXPIRED ? (isPA ? "SURVIVED" : "EXPIRED") : "WAITING"

fmtMoney(float v) =>
    na(v) ? "-" : str.tostring(v, "#,##0")

medianText(array<float> a) =>
    a.size() > 0 ? str.tostring(a.median(), "#.#") : "-"

var table tb = table.new(position.top_right, 8, 12, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 12), frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 50), frame_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 70), border_width = 1)

cell(int c, int r, string txt, color tc) =>
    table.cell(tb, c, r, txt, text_color = tc, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_center)

// Finished attempts only (the running one is in the current-attempt rows).
// PA: Expired counts attempts that survived the horizon; rate = breached share.
statsRow(int r, string ledgerName, string sample, Ledger L, int si) =>
    int ps = L.nPassed.get(si)
    int br = L.nBreached.get(si)
    int ex = L.nExpired.get(si)
    int done = ps + br + ex
    array<float> days = si == 0 ? L.daysIS : L.daysOOS
    color fg = color.new(color.white, 0)
    cell(0, r, ledgerName, color.new(color.silver, 0))
    cell(1, r, sample, color.new(color.silver, 0))
    cell(2, r, str.tostring(done), fg)
    cell(3, r, isPA ? "-" : str.tostring(ps), fg)
    cell(4, r, str.tostring(br), fg)
    cell(5, r, str.tostring(ex), fg)
    cell(6, r, done > 0 ? str.tostring(100.0 * (isPA ? br : ps) / done, "#.#") : "-", fg)
    cell(7, r, medianText(days), fg)

currentRow(int r, string ledgerName, Ledger L, float equityNow) =>
    color fg = color.new(color.white, 0)
    float room = equityNow - L.threshold
    string modeTxt = isPA ? "PA L" + str.tostring(L.tier) + (L.dllHit ? " DLL" : "") + " | session " + str.tostring(L.sessions) + "/" + str.tostring(iPaHorizon) : na(planStopLevel) ? "EVAL (no stop)" : "EVAL (stop " + fmtMoney(planStopLevel) + ")"
    cell(0, r, ledgerName, color.new(color.silver, 0))
    cell(1, r, fmtMoney(equityNow), fg)
    cell(2, r, fmtMoney(L.peak), fg)
    cell(3, r, fmtMoney(L.threshold), fg)
    cell(4, r, fmtMoney(room), fg)
    cell(5, r, statusText(L.status), fg)
    cell(6, r, modeTxt, fg)
    cell(7, r, str.tostring(L.tradedDays), fg)

// Raw trades mode: one row of per-trade results for a ledger and sample.
rawRow(int r, string ledgerName, string sample, RawStats S, int si) =>
    int n = S.n.get(si)
    float gl = S.grossLoss.get(si)
    float gw = S.grossWin.get(si)
    color fg = color.new(color.white, 0)
    cell(0, r, ledgerName, color.new(color.silver, 0))
    cell(1, r, sample, color.new(color.silver, 0))
    cell(2, r, str.tostring(n), fg)
    cell(3, r, n > 0 ? str.tostring(100.0 * S.wins.get(si) / n, "#.#") : "-", fg)
    cell(4, r, n > 0 ? str.tostring(S.perContract.get(si) / n, "#,##0.00") : "-", fg)
    cell(5, r, n == 0 ? "-" : gl > 0 ? str.tostring(gw / gl, "#.##") : "no losses", fg)
    cell(6, r, n > 0 ? fmtMoney(S.net.get(si)) : "-", fg)

// Size warning ("" = none): the July min stop cannot buy one contract at this
// risk (so every July setup is skipped), or the strategy has taken no entry
// while signals were skipped for size.
sizeWarnText(int skipped) =>
    float julyMinRisk = iMinStop * pv + rtCost
    string fix = isMicro ? "." : " or chart the micro (e.g. MNQ)."
    string w = ""
    if iSource == SRC_JULY and iMinStop > 0 and iRisk < julyMinRisk
        w := "Risk per trade $" + str.tostring(iRisk, "#") + " cannot buy 1 " + syminfo.root + " at the July min stop (" + str.tostring(iMinStop, "#.##") + " pt x $" + str.tostring(pv, "#.##") + " + $" + str.tostring(rtCost, "0.00") + " = $" + str.tostring(julyMinRisk, "0.00") + "): EVERY July setup is skipped. Raise Risk per trade to at least $" + str.tostring(math.ceil(julyMinRisk), "#") + fix
    else if strategy.closedtrades + strategy.opentrades == 0 and skipped > 0
        w := "No entries: every signal (" + str.tostring(skipped) + ") was skipped for size < 1. Raise Risk per trade" + fix
    w

if barstate.islast and iShowTable and not isRaw
    string sigName = iSource == SRC_RAND ? "Strategy (random)" : iSource == SRC_EXT ? "External" : "July setups"
    string oosTxt = str.format_time(iOOS, "yyyy-MM-dd", TZ)
    color hd = color.new(color.orange, 0)
    color nt = color.new(color.gray, 10)
    table.clear(tb, 0, 0, 7, 11)
    cell(0, 0, "Apex 50K Eval Lab | " + (isPA ? "Performance Account" : "Evaluation, " + iFeed) + " | " + iExit + " | " + (favFirst ? "favorable-first marks" : "adverse-first marks"), hd)
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 0, 7, 0)
    cell(0, 1, "Ledger", hd)
    cell(1, 1, "Sample", hd)
    cell(2, 1, "Attempts", hd)
    cell(3, 1, "Passed", hd)
    cell(4, 1, "Breached", hd)
    cell(5, 1, isPA ? "Survived " + str.tostring(iPaHorizon) : "Expired", hd)
    cell(6, 1, isPA ? "Breach %" : "Pass %", hd)
    cell(7, 1, isPA ? "Med days to breach" : "Med days to pass", hd)
    statsRow(2, sigName, "In-sample", sigL, 0)
    statsRow(3, sigName, "OOS from " + oosTxt, sigL, 1)
    statsRow(4, "Random control", "In-sample", rndL, 0)
    statsRow(5, "Random control", "OOS from " + oosTxt, rndL, 1)
    cell(0, 6, "Current attempt", hd)
    cell(1, 6, "Balance", hd)
    cell(2, 6, "Peak", hd)
    cell(3, 6, "Threshold", hd)
    cell(4, 6, "Room", hd)
    cell(5, 6, "Status", hd)
    cell(6, 6, "Mode / tier", hd)
    cell(7, 6, "Traded days", hd)
    currentRow(7, sigName, sigL, sBClose)
    currentRow(8, "Random control", rndL, rBClose)
    string costTxt = "Lab costs $" + str.tostring(commSide, "#.##") + "/side/contract (" + (iCommMode == COMM_AUTO ? (isMicro ? "auto: micro" : "auto: mini") : "custom") + "), slippage 1 tick, risk $" + str.tostring(iRisk, "#") + "/trade, cap " + str.tostring(sigL.planCap(qtyPerMini, iMaxQty)) + " " + syminfo.root + ".\nRandom control: p=" + str.tostring(iRndProb, "#.###") + ", stop " + str.tostring(iRndAtr, "#.##") + " ATR, " + (rndStopFirst ? "stop-first" : "TV path") + ", seed " + str.tostring(iSeed) + "."
    cell(0, 9, costTxt, nt)
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 9, 7, 9)
    string ambTxt = "Bars touching stop and target: signals " + str.tostring(sigL.ambiguous) + " (TradingView path decided), random " + str.tostring(rndL.ambiguous) + " (" + (rndStopFirst ? "stop-first" : "TV path") + ").\nSignal bars skipped for size < 1: signals " + str.tostring(sigL.skippedSize) + ", random " + str.tostring(rndL.skippedSize) + ". Entries: " + str.tostring(sigL.entries) + " / " + str.tostring(rndL.entries) + "."
    string sizeWarn = sizeWarnText(sigL.skippedSize)
    if sizeWarn != ""
        ambTxt += "\n" + sizeWarn
    cell(0, 10, ambTxt, sizeWarn != "" ? color.new(color.yellow, 0) : nt)
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 10, 7, 10)
    cell(0, 11, "Rules: Apex 50K Intraday, verified 2026-11-01. Lab only, not advice.", color.new(color.silver, 0))
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 11, 7, 11)

if barstate.islast and iShowTable and isRaw
    string sigName = iSource == SRC_RAND ? "Strategy (random)" : iSource == SRC_EXT ? "External" : "July setups"
    string oosTxt = str.format_time(iOOS, "yyyy-MM-dd", TZ)
    color hd = color.new(color.orange, 0)
    color nt = color.new(color.gray, 10)
    string flatTxt = str.tostring(math.floor(flatByMin / 60), "00") + ":" + str.tostring(flatByMin % 60, "00")
    table.clear(tb, 0, 0, 7, 11)
    cell(0, 0, "Apex 50K Eval Lab | Raw trades (no account rules) | " + iExit + " | " + (favFirst ? "favorable-first marks" : "adverse-first marks"), hd)
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 0, 6, 0)
    cell(0, 1, "Ledger", hd)
    cell(1, 1, "Sample", hd)
    cell(2, 1, "Trades", hd)
    cell(3, 1, "Win %", hd)
    cell(4, 1, "Net/trade/contract", hd)
    cell(5, 1, "Profit factor", hd)
    cell(6, 1, "Net P&L", hd)
    rawRow(2, sigName, "In-sample", sigRaw, 0)
    rawRow(3, sigName, "OOS from " + oosTxt, sigRaw, 1)
    rawRow(4, "Random control", "In-sample", rndRaw, 0)
    rawRow(5, "Random control", "OOS from " + oosTxt, rndRaw, 1)
    string costTxt = "Lab costs $" + str.tostring(commSide, "#.##") + "/side/contract (" + (iCommMode == COMM_AUTO ? (isMicro ? "auto: micro" : "auto: mini") : "custom") + "), slippage 1 tick, risk $" + str.tostring(iRisk, "#") + "/trade, cap " + str.tostring(rawCap) + " " + syminfo.root + ", flat-by " + flatTxt + " ET" + (flatByMin > 16 * 60 + 40 ? " (Tradeify exports: 16:40)" : "") + ".\nRandom control: p=" + str.tostring(iRndProb, "#.###") + ", stop " + str.tostring(iRndAtr, "#.##") + " ATR, " + (rndStopFirst ? "stop-first" : "TV path") + ", seed " + str.tostring(iSeed) + "."
    cell(0, 6, costTxt, nt)
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 6, 6, 6)
    string noteTxt = "A trade is one position (exit legs summed), net of lab costs; per contract = mean of each trade's net P&L / its contracts. The export's P&L uses the Properties-tab commission.\nSignal bars skipped for size < 1: signals " + str.tostring(sigL.skippedSize) + ", random " + str.tostring(rndL.skippedSize) + ". Bars touching stop and target: signals " + str.tostring(sigL.ambiguous) + ", random " + str.tostring(rndL.ambiguous) + "."
    cell(0, 7, noteTxt, nt)
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 7, 6, 7)
    color wc = color.new(color.yellow, 0)
    int r = 8
    if exitJuly
        cell(0, r, "Exit model is July playbook: the List of trades has one row per exit leg, and the planner sizes, caps and steps each row on its own (not the combined position), so it overstates size and understates breach risk. Set Exit model = Fixed R before exporting.", wc)
        table.merge_cells(tb, 0, r, 6, r)
        r += 1
    string sizeWarn = sizeWarnText(sigL.skippedSize)
    if sizeWarn != ""
        cell(0, r, sizeWarn, wc)
        table.merge_cells(tb, 0, r, 6, r)
        r += 1
    cell(0, r, "Export Strategy Tester > List of trades > Export as list.csv, then run: node planner/cli.mjs --firm tradeify --plan growth --trades list.csv --unit " + (isMicro ? "micro" : "mini") + " --sweep --scale risk", color.new(color.aqua, 0))
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, r, 6, r)
    cell(0, r + 1, "Raw trades: no attempts, no account rules; the planner applies the firm's rules. Lab only, not advice.", color.new(color.silver, 0))
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, r + 1, 6, r + 1)
